{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And if his offering is a sacrifice of peace offerings, etc. — whether male or female</b>. The reason in the burnt offering is that it be male, in the peace offerings that they be either male or female, and in the sin offering that it be female, is a clear matter, for the burnt offering is as its name, and the peace offerings are from the language of \"and all My desire I will fulfill\" (Isaiah 44:28), \"whole stones\" (Deuteronomy 27:6), and the sin offering is to propitiate His face with the meal offering that goes before it, and I have already written this (Genesis 46:1). And the guilt offering is male because the sin offering in cases liable to karet, since the soul returns to the Elohim who gave it, whereas the guilt offering does not come for an obligation of karet, and it is as though it is for a sweet savor like a burnt offering. And the goat of the nasi is because he is the ruler who holds justice and who fights the wars of HaShem and by whose sword he lives, in the manner of the goats of idolatry."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:50:02.049120553Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}